            {
              "text": "When setting up comprehensive estate planning documents—particularly **testamentary discretionary trusts** (for tax efficiency and asset protection) and **Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOAs)**—it is important to work with lawyers experienced in Queensland succession law, trust structuring, and tax implications.\n\nThe leading law firms and practitioners in and around **North Lakes** and **Chermside** (including immediate neighbouring suburbs such as Aspley and Nundah) represent strong options for these services:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Top Firms in North Lakes**\n\n#### **Cooke & Hutchinson Lawyers**\n* **Location:** North Lakes Central, 53 Endeavour Boulevard, North Lakes\n* **Specialties:** Comprehensive estate planning, testamentary trust drafting, Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOA), and Advance Health Directives (AHD).\n* **Why them:** Cooke & Hutchinson has a long-standing local presence. Their wills and estates division handles complex family situations, blended families, and business asset structures requiring testamentary discretionary trusts.\n\n#### **Zande Law**\n* **Location:** North Lakes\n* **Specialties:** Standard and complex wills, powers of attorney, estate administration, and retirement village transitions.\n* **Why them:** Established in 2007, Zande Law is the longest-operating independent law firm in North Lakes. They have a reputation for practical, plain-English advice and personal service for local families and seniors.\n\n#### **Cornerstone Law Offices**\n* **Location:** North Lakes (with offices across Greater Brisbane)\n* **Specialties:** Estate planning packages, drafting wills, testamentary trusts, and EPOAs.\n* **Why them:** Known for transparent fixed pricing and high client satisfaction. They provide tailored solutions whether you need a straightforward appointment of attorney or protective testamentary trusts for younger beneficiaries.\n\n#### **North Brisbane Law**\n* **Location:** North Lakes Office (also in Everton Park)\n* **Specialties:** Wills, probate, and enduring powers of attorney.\n* **Why them:** A dedicated Northside firm that focuses on ensuring estate documents are fully compliant with the *Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (Qld)* and the *Succession Act 1981 (Qld)* to prevent future disputes.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Top Firms in Chermside & Immediate Environs (Aspley / Nundah)**\n\n#### **Vicca Law** *(Aspley – 5 minutes from Chermside)*\n* **Location:** Aspley / North Brisbane\n* **Specialties:** Wills, estate planning, testamentary trusts, estate administration, and litigation.\n* **Why them:** Vicca Law stands out on Brisbane’s Northside for boutique, specialized attention to succession law. They have particular expertise in structuring testamentary trusts for capital protection, vulnerable beneficiaries, and tax effectiveness.\n\n#### **Kelly Lawyers** *(Servicing Chermside, Kedron, and Ascot)*\n* **Location:** Racecourse Road, Ascot (regularly services clients across Chermside and surrounding northern suburbs)\n* **Specialties:** Advanced estate planning, testamentary discretionary trusts, corporate/SMSF succession, and EPOAs.\n* **Why them:** If your estate involves company titles, family discretionary trusts, or self-managed super funds (SMSFs), Kelly Lawyers is strong in coordinating personal wills with broader entity succession.\n\n#### **Terry Anderssen Lawyers** *(Nundah – adjacent to Chermside)*\n* **Location:** Sandgate Road, Nundah\n* **Specialties:** Wills, Enduring Powers of Attorney, and probate.\n* **Why them:** Decades of experience in northern Brisbane suburban practice. They are well-regarded for guiding clients through the intricacies of choosing the right attorneys, setting up conditional powers, and drafting clear testamentary directions.\n\n---\n\n### **Key Considerations When Instructing Your Lawyer**\n\n1. **Testamentary Trusts vs. Standard Wills:**\n   * Make sure your lawyer clarifies whether a **testamentary discretionary trust (TDT)** is cost-effective for your asset level. TDTs provide significant income tax advantages for minor beneficiaries (taxed at adult marginal rates under s102AG of the ITAA 1936) and insulate inheritances from divorce or bankruptcy.\n2. **Assets Outside the Will:**\n   * Remind your lawyer to review assets that do *not* automatically pass under a Will—such as jointly held real estate, family trusts, and superannuation death benefits (which require binding death benefit nominations).\n3. **Enduring Power of Attorney Setup:**\n   * In Queensland, an EPOA allows you to appoint attorneys for **financial matters** (which can begin immediately or upon loss of capacity) and **personal/health matters** (which only take effect when capacity is lost). Ask whether you need joint, joint and several, or majority decision-making terms, and whether customized conditions/limitations should be included.\n4. **Accredited Specialists:**\n   * If your family or asset structure is particularly contentious or complex, ask if a lawyer who is a **Queensland Law Society (QLS) Accredited Specialist in Succession Law** will be drafting or reviewing the documentation.",
